WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.249 --> 00:00:02.300
This is a sample of what I got in the mail.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.058
It just comes in a plain envelope.

00:00:04.058 --> 00:00:07.069
Inside are these pills.

00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:11.900
Elisa Wells is a public health specialist
and the cofounder of PlanCPills.org.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.000
We are an information campaign to spread awareness

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.510
about all of the different ways that
they can be obtained in the United States

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:22.241
including in states that have restrictions
to access.

00:00:22.241 --> 00:00:25.300
For nearly 50 years, the US Supreme Court
held that

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.245
Americans had a general right to abortion.

00:00:28.245 --> 00:00:30.800
But individual states had power to decide
how difficult

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.557
the path to getting one would be.

00:00:33.557 --> 00:00:36.120
Over time, some states cleared the way

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:41.419
eventually even offering multiple routes like
telehealth, in-clinic, and mail-order options.

00:00:41.419 --> 00:00:46.238
Others made it much harder by adding obstacles
like waiting periods, mandatory ultrasounds

00:00:46.238 --> 00:00:50.237
counseling, and limiting abortions to
extremely early in pregnancy.

00:00:50.237 --> 00:00:53.696
Mississippi even forced doctors 
to mislead patients.

00:00:53.696 --> 00:00:56.720
The worst one that really 
makes me crazy is that

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.039
we have to tell them that

00:00:58.039 --> 00:01:01.438
it increases your risk of breast cancer 
and it doesn't.

00:01:01.438 --> 00:01:04.096
Just a complete lie.

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:08.460
But in June of 2022, the Supreme Court 
overturned Roe v. Wade

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.340
and now states can ban abortion completely.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.621
Many already have.

00:01:13.621 --> 00:01:17.422
There are a few key differences between now
and 50 years ago, though.

00:01:17.422 --> 00:01:21.194
One of them is this path: The abortion pill.

00:01:21.194 --> 00:01:25.780
Medication approved by the FDA to be delivered
by mail and taken at home.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.065
Safe, private, and effective.

00:01:29.065 --> 00:01:31.590
Accessing the pills isn't easy for everyone

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:35.113
but there are multiple paths people are taking
to get them.

00:01:35.113 --> 00:01:38.024
Because even states with the most restrictive
abortion laws

00:01:38.024 --> 00:01:42.245
have had trouble stopping medication
that’s discreetly shipped to your door.

00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:46.595
[pensive cello music]

00:01:46.595 --> 00:01:50.590
Medication abortion was approved for use in
the US in 2000.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:54.562
Today, it accounts for over half of legal
abortions in the nation.

00:01:54.562 --> 00:01:57.890
Any kind of serious side effect is less than
1%.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:01.369
So very safe and very effective.

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:03.599
While it’s often called 
“the abortion pill”

00:02:03.599 --> 00:02:05.810
it’s actually two medications

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:10.009
prescribed by a doctor to be taken within
the first 10 weeks of pregnancy

00:02:10.009 --> 00:02:14.455
though the World Health Organization says
it’s safe to use up to 12 weeks.

00:02:14.455 --> 00:02:17.650
In states where abortion is banned, it's now
illegal for doctors

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.569
to prescribe these pills for that purpose.

00:02:20.569 --> 00:02:24.675
But restricting or banning abortion doesn’t
eliminate the need for it.

00:02:24.675 --> 00:02:27.532
Whether something is legal or not doesn't
necessarily affect

00:02:27.532 --> 00:02:30.000
whether somebody makes a decision to
do something.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.790
It can affect what pathways they go to doing it.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.400
So here are four of those paths that people
are taking

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.280
to seek abortions as of July 2022.

00:02:40.186 --> 00:02:43.659
A woman in northern Mississippi named Kate
finds out she’s pregnant.

00:02:43.659 --> 00:02:46.129
She already has 3 children 
and knows she can’t afford

00:02:46.129 --> 00:02:48.220
to properly care for a fourth.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:49.267
That's a common refrain.

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:52.300
Just wanting to do the best they can for the
kids that they have.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:58.829
I think we're likely going to see folks 
get care in other states.

00:02:58.829 --> 00:03:00.300
Kate considers leaving Mississippi

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:04.050
and finding care in a state where abortion
is legal.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:07.510
The state of Mississippi could try 
to prosecute her if they find out

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:10.490
but it’s unlikely they’ll be successful.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:15.000
States typically only have power to enforce laws 
within their own borders.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:20.220
Unfortunately, the next closest option is
Illinois, which is too far to travel.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.838
So she explores other options.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.129
She recently read an article about a woman
who was able

00:03:25.129 --> 00:03:28.699
to get abortion pills mailed her to using
mail forwarding.

00:03:28.699 --> 00:03:33.769
And the way that works is, you know, supposing
you live in Arizona

00:03:33.769 --> 00:03:36.769
which is another state that has restrictions
on access

00:03:36.769 --> 00:03:39.930
you could look at the map 
on our website that shows

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:43.266
the states nearby that offer a telehealth
service.

00:03:43.266 --> 00:03:46.620
And you could say, oh, California has a lot
of telehealth services.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:47.980
They're right next to me.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:53.750
The provider in California is legally required
to only serve patients in California.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:58.879
I'm going to set up a virtual address in California.

00:03:58.879 --> 00:04:02.289
She looks at PostScanMail.com to see if this
is possible.

00:04:02.289 --> 00:04:05.325
A virtual mailbox could allow her to have
an appointment with an online provider

00:04:05.325 --> 00:04:08.189
like HeyJane or Just the Pill.

00:04:08.189 --> 00:04:14.000
You do a telehealth consultation with one
of the groups that serves California.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:21.768
And when they ask you for your mailing address,
you put in your virtual mailing address

00:04:21.768 --> 00:04:24.828
So far, this is Kate's best option.

00:04:24.828 --> 00:04:28.290
Another way we know people are finding pills
in the United States

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:33.888
is through online pharmacies and Plan C regularly
tests these pharmacies.

00:04:33.888 --> 00:04:37.880
These recommended online pharmacies often
offer expedited shipping

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:42.433
but aren’t approved by the FDA and can be expensive.

00:04:42.433 --> 00:04:44.600
Kate’s not sure she can come up with the
money for that

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:50.840
so she looks into another online provider:
this one isn’t located in the US.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:56.990
In a condition where access is totally cut
off, people will look for alternative ways

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:58.340
to access the pills.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:04.390
And we do know that Aid Access will still
be serving all 50 states.

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:09.370
Aid Access is run by a European doctor, offers
a sliding payment scale, and support for people

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:12.000
who want to self-manage abortion.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.240
They also allow pre-orders of the medication.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:18.943
But shipping times can take up to 3 weeks
from Europe.

00:05:18.943 --> 00:05:23.031
Kate weighs her options, but knows all of
them carry potential legal risks.

00:05:23.031 --> 00:05:25.610
We don't think that people 
are doing anything wrong

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:30.000
when they access pills through these 
alternative sources.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:36.090
But we do know that people have been criminalized
for self-managing an abortion.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:40.675
If anyone has questions about, you know, is
it legal in my state, what can I do?

00:05:40.675 --> 00:05:42.380
What are my risks for criminalization?

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:47.280
I encourage them to reach out to our repro
legal helpline because that's exactly what

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:52.020
we're there for, where attorneys in a 
confidential conversation can talk to you

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.179
about what your legal risks are.

00:05:55.350 --> 00:06:00.880
By the time you’re watching this, laws around
each of these options may have already changed.

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:04.150
Kate decides the best path for her is mail
forwarding

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:07.201
but others will choose the best route for
their own circumstances.

00:06:09.367 --> 00:06:13.860
Abortion with pills has really changed the
landscape of how people can end their pregnancy

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:17.877
safely at home without the involvement of
a clinic.

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:19.894
And the studies have shown that to be true.

00:06:19.894 --> 00:06:25.230
It is safe, it is effective, and it's a way
for you to get the care that you deserve

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.740
to have in the United States of America 
right now.

00:06:28.361 --> 00:06:30.260
You know, you got to make the best decision
for you.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:31.289
You’ve got to consider your health.

00:06:31.289 --> 00:06:32.480
You’ve got to consider your family.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.530
You’ve got to consider your career.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:36.771
You’ve got to consider your other kids.

00:06:36.771 --> 00:06:38.611
That's all any of us can do.

